WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.310 --> 00:00:05.549
Given how wild and unpredictable the world
can be, wouldn’t life be so much easier

00:00:05.549 --> 00:00:07.850
if we could see into the future?

00:00:07.850 --> 00:00:13.330
Imagine being able to look ahead and know
what good or bad thing is about to come around

00:00:13.330 --> 00:00:14.330
the corner.

00:00:14.330 --> 00:00:18.820
If times have been hard for you, knowing you’ve
got something worth looking forward to might

00:00:18.820 --> 00:00:21.509
give you just enough willpower to keep going.

00:00:21.509 --> 00:00:26.439
Or if there’s a storm on the horizon, then
at least you would have enough time to prepare.

00:00:26.439 --> 00:00:31.669
Unfortunately, being able to glimpse at future
events is a power that only a few – if any

00:00:31.669 --> 00:00:33.740
– of us are blessed with.

00:00:33.740 --> 00:00:38.970
Ask a cynic and they might tell you that seeing
the future is an ability reserved for scammers

00:00:38.970 --> 00:00:44.890
and con artists at fairgrounds or selling
out magic shows in Las Vegas; all people just

00:00:44.890 --> 00:00:50.280
trying to make a quick buck by telling their
paying customers what they want to hear.

00:00:50.280 --> 00:00:54.260
You can’t part the cloudy veil that hangs
over the future for free, after all.

00:00:54.260 --> 00:00:59.940
And then there are fortune cookies, those
crispy, sugary treats you crack open after

00:00:59.940 --> 00:01:04.509
a meal, usually containing a piece of paper
with some pre-written, generic aphorism or

00:01:04.509 --> 00:01:06.130
a vague prophecy.

00:01:06.130 --> 00:01:12.020
If a human being can’t look into the future,
then surely those ambiguous predictions printed

00:01:12.020 --> 00:01:16.899
on tiny slips of paper and left inside of
fortune cookies could never be accurate…

00:01:16.899 --> 00:01:17.899
right?

00:01:17.899 --> 00:01:19.520
Sage was one of the cynics.

00:01:19.520 --> 00:01:25.210
Sure, some might argue he had every right
to be, having fallen on some pretty hard times.

00:01:25.210 --> 00:01:30.010
Things weren’t exactly running smoothly,
and his life certainly had not taken the direction

00:01:30.010 --> 00:01:31.819
that he hoped it would.

00:01:31.819 --> 00:01:37.530
The trouble had started when, quite unexpectedly,
his landlord had raised the rent on his apartment.

00:01:37.530 --> 00:01:41.640
Sage had been struggling to make ends meet
at work already, and the increase in those

00:01:41.640 --> 00:01:44.380
monthly payments meant his hands were tied.

00:01:44.380 --> 00:01:49.340
Eventually, he had no choice but to move out,
forced by the increase in rent to leave the

00:01:49.340 --> 00:01:51.920
apartment he had once called home.

00:01:51.920 --> 00:01:57.249
The one saving grace was that his friends,
Ash and Joey, had offered him a place to stay,

00:01:57.249 --> 00:02:00.820
as long as Sage could throw them a little
bit of money to cover their own rent.

00:02:00.820 --> 00:02:05.470
It was way less than his old landlord was
asking for, however even that came with an

00:02:05.470 --> 00:02:09.830
unfortunate downside; the caveat that Sage
would have to sleep on their couch instead

00:02:09.830 --> 00:02:11.340
of having his own room.

00:02:11.340 --> 00:02:14.681
Sure, not the worst thing in the world, but
it does beat the floor.

00:02:14.681 --> 00:02:18.540
But for Sage, it was far from an ideal living
situation.

00:02:18.540 --> 00:02:23.230
To try and lessen the blow of having to leave
the independence and privacy of his own place,

00:02:23.230 --> 00:02:27.430
Joey and Ash had decided amongst themselves
to throw a little celebratory dinner.

00:02:27.430 --> 00:02:31.010
But of course, the key oversight to their
plan was that neither of them were all that

00:02:31.010 --> 00:02:35.769
great at cooking, mostly surviving either
on ordering in delivery from local fast food

00:02:35.769 --> 00:02:41.340
places, or anything that only needed a quick
nuking in the microwave in order to be made

00:02:41.340 --> 00:02:42.340
edible.

00:02:42.340 --> 00:02:46.310
All the same, Ash was adamant that their lack
of culinary know-how wasn’t going to stand

00:02:46.310 --> 00:02:47.310
in their way.

00:02:47.310 --> 00:02:51.300
He and his fellow roommate were going to lay
on a slap-up feast for their down on his luck

00:02:51.300 --> 00:02:55.840
friend, Sage, the only way they knew how:
by ordering takeout.

00:02:55.840 --> 00:03:01.120
“It’s… food,” he remarked, a little
lost for words after having seen his two new

00:03:01.120 --> 00:03:05.819
roommates excitedly yelling ‘surprise’
at him the moment he walked through the door.

00:03:05.819 --> 00:03:09.710
“Not just any food,” Joey replied, grinning
like a maniac.

00:03:09.710 --> 00:03:11.920
“It’s ‘welcome to the apartment’ food!”

00:03:11.920 --> 00:03:17.159
“You wanted to celebrate me sleeping on
your couch,” Sage said, staring at the mountains

00:03:17.159 --> 00:03:21.829
of white paper oyster pails on the table with
red Mandarin lettering and ancient temples

00:03:21.829 --> 00:03:23.310
painted on the sides.

00:03:23.310 --> 00:03:27.040
“By ordering Chinese food?” he added with
confusion.

00:03:27.040 --> 00:03:31.610
“Look, you’ve been going through it man,”
Ash cut in, explaining things that Sage already

00:03:31.610 --> 00:03:32.610
knew.

00:03:32.610 --> 00:03:34.670
“So, we figured this might lift your spirits.

00:03:34.670 --> 00:03:38.150
Check it out, we’ve got it all here man,
dumplings, noodles, the works!

00:03:38.150 --> 00:03:39.180
And for after…”

00:03:39.180 --> 00:03:44.430
He produced a small box, the brand name ‘La
Choy’ emblazoned on its surface.

00:03:44.430 --> 00:03:48.990
Inside were twelve fortune cookies, all individually
wrapped for freshness as the writing on the

00:03:48.990 --> 00:03:50.090
box boasted.

00:03:50.090 --> 00:03:52.650
“Hey, maybe you’ll get some good news
from one of these!”

00:03:52.650 --> 00:03:55.620
Joey smiled, pointing at the box.

00:03:55.620 --> 00:03:59.579
“I… thanks guys,” Sage eventually said,
chuckling quietly to himself.

00:03:59.579 --> 00:04:04.180
He had to admit, what his friends were trying
to do for him, albeit a little excessive,

00:04:04.180 --> 00:04:06.590
came from a place of good intentions.

00:04:06.590 --> 00:04:12.189
Little did any of them know it was about to
change the very course of their lives… their

00:04:12.189 --> 00:04:13.909
fortunes, forever.

00:04:13.909 --> 00:04:18.709
Nearly two hours and several pounds of greasy
Chinese takeout later, the trio of roommates

00:04:18.709 --> 00:04:22.290
were starting to wonder whether or not this
feast had been a good idea.

00:04:22.290 --> 00:04:26.780
What had started as an innocent meal now had
them all feeling a little queasy, having eaten

00:04:26.780 --> 00:04:31.690
so much that they were questioning their life
choices, and still with a few oyster pails

00:04:31.690 --> 00:04:34.000
half full of leftover food.

00:04:34.000 --> 00:04:38.200
Throwing out the empty paper containers and
leaving the rest in the fridge, Sage sat back

00:04:38.200 --> 00:04:43.220
on the sofa, groaning in tandem with his friends
and cursing himself for having a third helping

00:04:43.220 --> 00:04:44.420
of the chilli beef.

00:04:44.420 --> 00:04:49.680
“Oh, damn, I almost forgot,” Joey said
weakly, reaching for the box of fortune cookies.

00:04:49.680 --> 00:04:53.190
Opening it, he offered it to Sage, who immediately
put his hands up to refuse.

00:04:53.190 --> 00:04:58.070
“No way, if I eat another thing, I sweat
I might have a heart attack,” he said.

00:04:58.070 --> 00:05:03.610
“We don’t actually have to eat them,”
Ash interjected, picking up one of the plastic-wrapped

00:05:03.610 --> 00:05:04.610
cookies at random.

00:05:04.610 --> 00:05:06.401
“You only open them for the fortunes anyway.”

00:05:06.401 --> 00:05:10.810
“Right, and I guess one of these cookies
is going to tell me that ‘Everything happens

00:05:10.810 --> 00:05:15.919
for a reason’ or to ‘Keep my head up’,
or some other vague, non-specific prediction,”

00:05:15.919 --> 00:05:18.810
Sage replied, making no attempt to mask his
sarcasm.

00:05:18.810 --> 00:05:24.640
“Come on, man,” Joey urged, taking a cookie
himself before thrusting the box into Sage’s

00:05:24.640 --> 00:05:25.640
hands.

00:05:25.640 --> 00:05:28.940
“Sure, they’re never perfectly accurate,
but it’s just a bit of fun.

00:05:28.940 --> 00:05:33.210
Besides, it’s all down to how you interpret
your fortune, you aren’t meant to take it

00:05:33.210 --> 00:05:34.210
literally.”

00:05:34.210 --> 00:05:38.590
With a cynical sigh, Sage gave in and grabbed
one of the remaining fortune cookies.

00:05:38.590 --> 00:05:42.930
Tearing open the plastic packaging surrounding
it in time with Ash and Joey doing the same,

00:05:42.930 --> 00:05:45.789
he then snapped the yellow, sugary shell in
two.

00:05:45.789 --> 00:05:50.319
A tiny piece of paper was concealed within,
with an inscription printed on one side in

00:05:50.319 --> 00:05:51.319
blue ink.

00:05:51.319 --> 00:05:55.479
But before he had a chance to read it, Joey,
who was sitting next to him and had just done

00:05:55.479 --> 00:05:59.610
the same, recited his own fortune out loud:
“Buy a ticket, trust your instinct and the

00:05:59.610 --> 00:06:01.240
numbers will come,” he read.

00:06:01.240 --> 00:06:03.880
“No way that’s what it says,” Ash argued.

00:06:03.880 --> 00:06:05.800
“I’m not kidding,” Joey protested.

00:06:05.800 --> 00:06:10.240
“Let me guess, the other side reads ‘This
fortune was sponsored by the State Lottery’?”

00:06:10.240 --> 00:06:11.240
Sage joked.

00:06:11.240 --> 00:06:15.900
Indignantly, Joey held his fortune up to his
friends' faces, letting them read for themselves

00:06:15.900 --> 00:06:18.180
what he had already repeated aloud.

00:06:18.180 --> 00:06:22.430
Being far from a betting man, Joey had hardly
ever made as little as a friendly, low-stakes

00:06:22.430 --> 00:06:27.180
wager, let alone taken the chance on playing
either the State Lottery or a national one

00:06:27.180 --> 00:06:28.540
like the Powerball.

00:06:28.540 --> 00:06:31.470
The odds of winning just seemed like they
were stacked too high.

00:06:31.470 --> 00:06:36.039
And yet, something about just how specific
this fortune was made Joey feel compelled

00:06:36.039 --> 00:06:40.460
to maybe give it a try, considering taking
a chance and playing against those odds by

00:06:40.460 --> 00:06:42.180
buying himself a ticket.

00:06:42.180 --> 00:06:47.080
“My turn,” Ash announced, excitedly unfolding
her own paper fortune and clearing her throat.

00:06:47.080 --> 00:06:50.810
“Keep your light on, the person you’re
looking for will be here soon.”

00:06:50.810 --> 00:06:54.830
Even someone as cynical as Sage had to admit
there was something very strange about how

00:06:54.830 --> 00:06:58.780
detailed these fortunes had been – or seemed
to be, at least.

00:06:58.780 --> 00:07:03.080
Part of him thought maybe that was part of
their gimmick, making the text on the paper

00:07:03.080 --> 00:07:08.420
that little bit less vague and generic than
those found in other cookies so that people

00:07:08.420 --> 00:07:12.199
would find it easier to believe they were
an accurate prediction of the future.

00:07:12.199 --> 00:07:16.220
But then again, it did seem like a strange
coincidence.

00:07:16.220 --> 00:07:20.050
Sage knew that Ash had been trying to get
back into the dating scene, but was having

00:07:20.050 --> 00:07:23.120
little luck on the more popular apps for meeting
new people.

00:07:23.120 --> 00:07:28.240
Still, it’s not like the prediction on that
little piece would actually come true, nor

00:07:28.240 --> 00:07:29.419
would Joey’s.

00:07:29.419 --> 00:07:34.130
But if nothing else, the least it could do
was inspire a little hope in the pair of them.

00:07:34.130 --> 00:07:37.849
Sage looked down at his own fortune, part
of him secretly wanting there to be another

00:07:37.849 --> 00:07:40.250
optimistic message written on the paper.

00:07:40.250 --> 00:07:44.990
After all, he needed a little boost in that
department, even if it was just for tonight.

00:07:44.990 --> 00:07:47.479
Printed in blue ink were just three short
words:

00:07:47.479 --> 00:07:52.700
“Look both ways,” Sage read, immediately
feeling his heart drop in disappointment.

00:07:52.700 --> 00:07:57.080
“That one sounds way vaguer,” Joey commented,
highlighting the obvious.

00:07:57.080 --> 00:08:02.610
“Well, we can’t all pick the nice fortunes,”
Sage retorted, screwing the tiny slip of paper

00:08:02.610 --> 00:08:05.170
up in his hand and stuffing it into his back
pocket.

00:08:05.170 --> 00:08:07.090
“They’re all just randomly generated anyway.

00:08:07.090 --> 00:08:10.780
There are probably a million fortunes out
there that are all worded exactly the same

00:08:10.780 --> 00:08:11.780
as ours.

00:08:11.780 --> 00:08:14.009
It’s not like any of these will come true
anyway.”

00:08:14.009 --> 00:08:18.720
Falling asleep on the couch later that night,
Sage had no idea just how wrong he was about

00:08:18.720 --> 00:08:20.090
to be proven.

00:08:20.090 --> 00:08:24.470
Almost to the same degree, he had little clue
as to what his fortune had actually meant,

00:08:24.470 --> 00:08:26.990
but would only realize when it was too late…

00:08:26.990 --> 00:08:30.789
Over the course of the following few months,
a lot seemed to be happening in the lives

00:08:30.789 --> 00:08:36.229
of Sage’s two friends; and by contrast,
very little was changing in his own life.

00:08:36.229 --> 00:08:40.300
The first surprise came when Ash had met a
new flame, a girl by the name of Skye.

00:08:40.300 --> 00:08:44.779
In Sage’s head, it was just a fling, not
something he expected to last – although

00:08:44.779 --> 00:08:49.209
he would think twice about saying it out loud
so as to not upset his roommate.

00:08:49.209 --> 00:08:54.460
But, to his surprise, Ash seemed to be utterly
smitten with her newfound relationship, the

00:08:54.460 --> 00:08:59.640
pair of them were happy, the very textbook
definition of head over heels for one another.

00:08:59.640 --> 00:09:03.861
Both Sage and Joey were quick to voice their
support, but seeing what Ash’s fortune cookie

00:09:03.861 --> 00:09:07.510
had predicted actually coming to pass got
the latter of them thinking.

00:09:07.510 --> 00:09:10.670
Had that just been a lucky coincidence?

00:09:10.670 --> 00:09:13.500
Was it just a case of right place, right time?

00:09:13.500 --> 00:09:17.680
Joey wasn’t entirely convinced, despite
Sage telling him otherwise.

00:09:17.680 --> 00:09:22.600
As far as he was concerned, it was all just
down to timing and confirmation bias.

00:09:22.600 --> 00:09:26.690
Something that was impossible to predict or
foresee had happened that just so happened

00:09:26.690 --> 00:09:30.050
to coincide with what they had read in their
fortune cookies.

00:09:30.050 --> 00:09:35.070
But for his friend, it seemed an awful lot
like the fortune Ash had picked was one hundred

00:09:35.070 --> 00:09:38.930
percent accurate, which meant he could be
too.

00:09:38.930 --> 00:09:43.070
On top of that, Joey couldn’t help but wonder,
had the fortunes inside the cookies predicted

00:09:43.070 --> 00:09:48.560
what was already going to happen, or did reading
those predictions make them become a reality?

00:09:48.560 --> 00:09:52.980
Eager to find out if his own fortune cookie
had been telling the truth, Joey decided to

00:09:52.980 --> 00:09:55.730
make a spontaneous venture on his way home
from work.

00:09:55.730 --> 00:09:59.839
While riding the subway, he opened up the
website for the Powerball and went about purchasing

00:09:59.839 --> 00:10:00.839
a ticket.

00:10:00.839 --> 00:10:05.480
The minimum bet was only a few dollars, but
if his cookie prophecy was really a guaranteed,

00:10:05.480 --> 00:10:10.579
accurate forecast of the future, then Joey
was in for good fortune in every literal sense

00:10:10.579 --> 00:10:11.660
of the word.

00:10:11.660 --> 00:10:16.740
His paper slip had told him to put faith in
his own instincts, and so, with trembling

00:10:16.740 --> 00:10:22.060
hands, he input a series of numbers, going
with the first ones that popped into his head.

00:10:22.060 --> 00:10:25.340
Getting back to the apartment that night,
Joey’s heart was racing, and he made sure

00:10:25.340 --> 00:10:27.450
to let the others know about it.

00:10:27.450 --> 00:10:31.640
Barely able to contain his excitement, the
pure unfiltered nervousness his friend was

00:10:31.640 --> 00:10:34.990
exhibiting quickly became unbearable to Sage.

00:10:34.990 --> 00:10:38.600
The draw for the Powerball was fast approaching
at the end of the week, although he was getting

00:10:38.600 --> 00:10:42.790
sick of Joey claiming his numbers were sure
to be called, and pondering out loud what

00:10:42.790 --> 00:10:44.710
he would spend the prize money on.

00:10:44.710 --> 00:10:48.889
Sage’s cynicism still prevented him from
believing that his friend was going to win,

00:10:48.889 --> 00:10:51.959
despite having witnessed Ash’s fortune come
true already.

00:10:51.959 --> 00:10:57.120
It wasn’t until it happened right in front
of his eyes that Sage started to realize just

00:10:57.120 --> 00:10:59.060
how wrong he might have been.

00:10:59.060 --> 00:11:02.800
The night of the draw, the three roommates
– plus the new love of Ash’s life – were

00:11:02.800 --> 00:11:04.540
gathered around the TV.

00:11:04.540 --> 00:11:08.580
All of them, apart from Sage, were glued to
the screen, barely breathing.

00:11:08.580 --> 00:11:13.700
The apartment was so quiet you could hear
a pin drop, the silence only broken by Sage

00:11:13.700 --> 00:11:15.430
occasionally piping up.

00:11:15.430 --> 00:11:19.220
“Watch, it’s not actually going to come
true,” he would assert, not intending to

00:11:19.220 --> 00:11:24.730
put a downer on the proceedings, but merely
trying to encourage Joey to manage his expectations.

00:11:24.730 --> 00:11:28.139
The other three shushed him; the numbers were
about to be called.

00:11:28.139 --> 00:11:31.829
Gripping his ticket in one hand, the paper
slip containing his fortune in the other,

00:11:31.829 --> 00:11:35.760
Joey felt his pulse rising, heart bumping
against his chest.

00:11:35.760 --> 00:11:40.589
He wasn’t sure if it was out of excitement,
or nerves; in fact, it was more likely an

00:11:40.589 --> 00:11:42.250
even blend of both.

00:11:42.250 --> 00:11:46.450
On the screen, the multi-colored balls were
pulled one by one out of a spinning chamber,

00:11:46.450 --> 00:11:48.360
each one marked with a different number.

00:11:48.360 --> 00:11:50.620
Slowly, the first was revealed to the audience.

00:11:50.620 --> 00:11:54.880
Joey, Ash, and her partner Skye could hardly
contain their excitement when they saw that

00:11:54.880 --> 00:11:57.949
it was the same as the first number Joey had
picked out.

00:11:57.949 --> 00:12:01.829
It was only when the second number was called,
and the others once again yelped in excitement

00:12:01.829 --> 00:12:05.980
so loudly that Sage looked up from his phone
and took notice.

00:12:05.980 --> 00:12:10.820
Before his very own eyes, he watched as each
number that the Powerball presenter unveiled

00:12:10.820 --> 00:12:14.839
was met with a chorus of more and more excited
whooping from his friends.

00:12:14.839 --> 00:12:19.890
They were all a perfect match for Joey’s
numbers, every single one.

00:12:19.890 --> 00:12:25.540
He had won a huge sum of money exactly as
the fortune cookie had alluded to.

00:12:25.540 --> 00:12:29.550
Even for someone as skeptical and disbelieving
of predicting the future, it was hard for

00:12:29.550 --> 00:12:33.380
Sage to deny that both his roommates’ fortunes
had come true.

00:12:33.380 --> 00:12:38.190
In fact, it was especially hard to be cynical
about it after watching firsthand as Joey

00:12:38.190 --> 00:12:42.890
won the Powerball by ‘trusting his instincts,
which boiled down to him literally picking

00:12:42.890 --> 00:12:45.790
the first numbers that randomly came into
his head.

00:12:45.790 --> 00:12:51.389
But given how specific both Joey’s and Ash’s
personal prophecies had been, compared to

00:12:51.389 --> 00:12:56.500
how vague his own was, Sage didn’t know
if what his slip of paper had said was a promise

00:12:56.500 --> 00:12:59.230
of good things to come, or an ominous warning.

00:12:59.230 --> 00:13:03.610
It also didn’t help that he just couldn’t
nail down what it meant.

00:13:03.610 --> 00:13:05.740
‘Look both ways.’

00:13:05.740 --> 00:13:08.860
For weeks and weeks on end, he mulled the
phrase over in his head.

00:13:08.860 --> 00:13:12.990
It didn’t make sense for it to be completely
literal, leading Sage to try and think of

00:13:12.990 --> 00:13:15.500
more metaphorical interpretations of his fortune.

00:13:15.500 --> 00:13:20.160
He thought maybe there was something political
about it, that it might be urging him to consider

00:13:20.160 --> 00:13:24.690
both of America’s two parties more equally
when casting a vote, rather than just blindly

00:13:24.690 --> 00:13:25.690
ticking a box.

00:13:25.690 --> 00:13:29.670
But the next election was still years away,
meanwhile, the predictions of Ash’s and

00:13:29.670 --> 00:13:33.750
Joey’s fortune cookies had already come
to pass in the six months since they had first

00:13:33.750 --> 00:13:34.839
opened them.

00:13:34.839 --> 00:13:39.199
Frustrated and looking for the exact answer
behind his paper fortune, Sage was running

00:13:39.199 --> 00:13:44.529
out of ways to reinterpret those three words
that apparently dictated his inevitable fate.

00:13:44.529 --> 00:13:49.800
But the thing that pushed him into pure desperation
was the uncontrollable jealousy of witnessing

00:13:49.800 --> 00:13:53.380
just how happy his friends were after their
fortunes became true.

00:13:53.380 --> 00:13:57.040
He wanted to be happy for them and tried his
best to be.

00:13:57.040 --> 00:14:00.990
But seeing Ash and Skye in their blissful
relationship, and Joey frivolously spending

00:14:00.990 --> 00:14:04.959
his Powerball winnings on expensive clothing
soon became unbearable.

00:14:04.959 --> 00:14:08.740
Having exhausted all other options, still
no closer to understanding what his fortune

00:14:08.740 --> 00:14:13.440
was, Sage decided to visit the Chinese restaurant
they had ordered their food from all those

00:14:13.440 --> 00:14:14.680
months ago.

00:14:14.680 --> 00:14:18.060
But his heart sank as the staff working in
the restaurant told him that whatever was

00:14:18.060 --> 00:14:22.529
written in the fortune cookies didn’t have
any bearing on the real world.

00:14:22.529 --> 00:14:24.459
“You don’t understand,” Sage argued.

00:14:24.459 --> 00:14:26.640
“My friends both had their fortunes come
true.

00:14:26.640 --> 00:14:31.029
I mean the cookies we got from you predicted
it almost perfectly, down to the word.

00:14:31.029 --> 00:14:33.820
I just need you to tell me what my one means!”

00:14:33.820 --> 00:14:36.930
“I’m sorry, sir,” the young man behind
the counter replied.

00:14:36.930 --> 00:14:39.550
“But it must just be a coincidence.

00:14:39.550 --> 00:14:42.810
Fortune cookies can’t accurately tell the
future, it’s more about what you believe

00:14:42.810 --> 00:14:44.000
the fortune means.”

00:14:44.000 --> 00:14:47.250
Disheartened, Sage left the restaurant, his
head hanging low.

00:14:47.250 --> 00:14:51.920
As he walked down the street towards the sidewalk,
he felt his phone vibrate in his pocket.

00:14:51.920 --> 00:14:54.670
Taking a look at the screen, still walking,
he saw a text from Joey.

00:14:54.670 --> 00:14:58.740
He was asking if Sage had any luck asking
the restaurant about his fortune cookie.

00:14:58.740 --> 00:15:02.600
Maybe if Sage had done what that fateful slip
of paper had told him, as he stepped off the

00:15:02.600 --> 00:15:06.829
sidewalk, then he would have seen the bus
speeding down the road towards him.

00:15:06.829 --> 00:15:10.910
If you want to know the future, perhaps you
should only look at your own risk.

00:15:10.910 --> 00:15:15.220
Sometimes knowing exactly what is destined
to happen to you can make it impossible to

00:15:15.220 --> 00:15:19.019
avoid, a self-fulfilling prophecy, if you
will.

00:15:19.019 --> 00:15:24.620
That is the warning given to any who dares
to take a prediction from SCP-377.

00:15:24.620 --> 00:15:29.440
Now residing in a personnel break room at
one of the SCP Foundation’s sites, SCP-377

00:15:29.440 --> 00:15:34.069
is the designation given to an anomalous box
of fortune cookies.

00:15:34.069 --> 00:15:37.990
The fact that the box is seemingly capable
of replenishing itself at regular intervals,

00:15:37.990 --> 00:15:43.389
refilling every twelve hours, happens to be
the far less interesting thing about it.

00:15:43.389 --> 00:15:46.850
Any of the fortune cookies taken from SCP-377
are…

00:15:46.850 --> 00:15:51.560
well, the cookies themselves are completely
ordinary by any and all metrics.

00:15:51.560 --> 00:15:55.839
They taste exactly as fortune cookies should
and they aren’t made of any ingredients

00:15:55.839 --> 00:15:57.860
apart from those you’d expect.

00:15:57.860 --> 00:16:03.160
But somehow, without fail, every single fortune
found within one of these crispy, confectionary

00:16:03.160 --> 00:16:07.500
clairvoyants manages to be one hundred percent
accurate.

00:16:07.500 --> 00:16:12.120
They aren’t generalized predictions for
the future, definitely, none of them have

00:16:12.120 --> 00:16:15.459
prophesized who the next winners of the World
Series are going to be, or who is next in

00:16:15.459 --> 00:16:17.180
line to be President.

00:16:17.180 --> 00:16:22.589
Every fortune contained in the SCP-377 cookies
are specifically tailored to the person who

00:16:22.589 --> 00:16:23.759
opens them.

00:16:23.759 --> 00:16:28.089
These fortunes have ranged from detailed foreknowledge
of upcoming events and changes in someone’s

00:16:28.089 --> 00:16:32.300
personal life, to vague, unspecified allusions
to what lies ahead.

00:16:32.300 --> 00:16:36.980
And, while always factually accurate and perfectly
aligned with the future, the predictions made

00:16:36.980 --> 00:16:40.970
by these cookies are not always promises of
good fortune.

00:16:40.970 --> 00:16:45.589
One researcher opened up an SCP-377 fortune
cookie only to read the phrase ‘It’s a

00:16:45.589 --> 00:16:46.589
boy’ written on the paper.

00:16:46.589 --> 00:16:52.440
Less than an hour later, his wife’s water
broke, and said researcher was soon welcoming

00:16:52.440 --> 00:16:55.269
his new-born baby son into the world.

00:16:55.269 --> 00:16:59.839
But another doctor was warned ‘You don’t
have long to live’, right before choking

00:16:59.839 --> 00:17:01.240
on his own cookie.

00:17:01.240 --> 00:17:05.700
Right there in the break room, that doctor
suffocated, killed by the same thing that

00:17:05.700 --> 00:17:08.420
foretold of his death only moments before.

00:17:08.420 --> 00:17:12.720
It is for that reason that SCP Foundation
personnel are given a warning before helping

00:17:12.720 --> 00:17:15.400
themselves to a sugary shelled treat.

00:17:15.400 --> 00:17:20.950
All staff are permitted to open a cookie from
SCP-377, after all, they are safe to eat.

00:17:20.950 --> 00:17:25.200
And Foundation employees are also welcome
to read their fortunes, however, they only

00:17:25.200 --> 00:17:28.220
do so at their own risk.

00:17:28.220 --> 00:17:34.460
Now go and check out “SCP-261 PAN DIMENSIONAL
VENDING MACHINE” and “SCP-348 A GIFT FROM

00:17:34.460 --> 00:17:38.820
DAD” if you’re still feeling peckish for
more appetizing anomalies and snack-worthy

00:17:38.820 --> 00:17:39.680
SCPs to satiate your hunger.

